{"id":"mahabharata-12-301","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":301,"title":"एकाधिकत्रिशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 301 · Self, objects and gods","summary":{"en":"Yajnavalkya explains that the feet are the inner self, going is the object and Vishnu the presiding god, and gives such triads for each of the organs of sense and action. He lists the qualities of sattva, rajas and tamas as they work in the body.","kn":"ಪಾದಗಳು ಅಧ್ಯಾತ್ಮ, ನಡೆಯುವುದು ಅಧಿಭೂತ, ವಿಷ್ಣು ಅಧಿದೈವ ಎಂದು ಯಾಜ್ಞವಲ್ಕ್ಯ ಹೇಳಿ ಪ್ರತಿ ಜ್ಞಾನೇಂದ್ರಿಯ-ಕರ್ಮೇಂದ್ರಿಯಕ್ಕೆ ಇಂತಹ ತ್ರಿಕಗಳನ್ನು ಕೊಡುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದೇಹದಲ್ಲಿ ಕಾರ್ಯ ಮಾಡುವ ಸತ್ತ್ವ, ರಜಸ್ಸು, ತಮಸ್ಸಿನ ಗುಣಗಳನ್ನು ಪಟ್ಟಿ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"याज्ञवल्क्य बताते हैं कि पाद अध्यात्म हैं, गमन अधिभूत है और विष्णु अधिदैवत हैं, और प्रत्येक ज्ञान-कर्म इन्द्रिय के ऐसे त्रिक देते हैं। वे देह में कार्य करने वाले सत्त्व, रजस् और तमस् के गुणों की सूची देते हैं।","te":"పాదాలు అధ్యాత్మం, నడక అధిభూతం, విష్ణువు అధిదైవతమని యాజ్ఞవల్క్యుడు చెప్పి ప్రతి జ్ఞాన కర్మేంద్రియానికి ఇలాంటి త్రికాలను ఇస్తాడు. దేహంలో పనిచేసే సత్త్వ రజస్ తమోగుణాలను పట్టిక చేస్తాడు.","ta":"பாதங்கள் அத்யாத்மம், நடை அதிபூதம், விஷ்ணு அதிதெய்வம் என்று யாஜ்ஞவல்க்யர் கூறி, ஒவ்வொரு அறிவு செயல் புலனுக்கும் இத்தகைய மூன்று கூறுகளைத் தருகிறார். உடலில் செயல்படும் சத்துவ ரஜஸ் தமஸ் குணங்களைப் பட்டியலிடுகிறார்.","ml":"യാജ്ഞവൽക്യൻ പറയുന്നു: പാദങ്ങൾ ഉള്ളിലെ ആത്മാവാണ്, നടത്തം വിഷയമാണ്, വിഷ്ണു അധിഷ്ഠാതാവായ ദേവനാണ്; ഇന്ദ്രിയങ്ങളിലും പ്രവർത്തനാവയവങ്ങളിലും ഓരോന്നിനും ഇങ്ങനെയുള്ള ത്രിത്വങ്ങൾ അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു. ശരീരത്തിൽ പ്രവർത്തിക്കുന്ന സത്ത്വം, രജസ്സ്, തമസ്സ് എന്നീ ഗുണങ്ങളുടെ വിവരണവും അദ്ദേഹം നൽകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.301; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"याज्ञवल्क्य उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yajnavalkya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"पादावध्यात्ममित्याहुर्ब्राह्मणास्तत्त्वदर्शिनः ।\nगन्तव्यमधिभूतं च विष्णुस्तत्राधिदैवतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins who see the truth call the feet the Self-related, what is to be gone to the elemental, and Vishnu the divinity there."}},{"n":2,"text":"पायुरध्यात्ममित्याहुर्यथातत्त्वार्थदर्शिनः ।\nविसर्गमधिभूतं च मित्रस्तत्राधिदैवतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who see the meaning of the principles call the organ of excretion the Self-related, discharge the elemental, and Mitra the divinity there."}},{"n":3,"text":"उपस्थोऽध्यात्ममित्याहुर्यथायोगनिदर्शनम् ।\nअधिभूतं तथानन्दो दैवतं च प्रजापतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Yoga teaches, the organ of generation is called Self-related, delight the elemental, and Prajapati the divinity."}},{"n":4,"text":"हस्तावध्यात्ममित्याहुर्यथासांख्यनिदर्शनम् ।\nकर्तव्यमधिभूतं तु इन्द्रस्तत्राधिदैवतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Sankhya teaches, the two hands are called Self-related, what is to be done the elemental, and Indra the divinity there."}},{"n":5,"text":"वागध्यात्ममिति प्राहुर्यथाश्रुतिनिदर्शनम् ।\nवक्तव्यमधिभूतं तु वह्निस्तत्राधिदैवतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the tradition teaches, speech is called Self-related, what is to be said the elemental, and Agni the divinity there."}},{"n":6,"text":"चक्षुरध्यात्ममित्याहुर्यथाश्रुतिनिदर्शनम् ।\nरूपमत्राधिभूतं तु सूर्यस्तत्राधिदैवतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the tradition teaches, the eye is called Self-related, form here the elemental, and the Sun the divinity there."}},{"n":7,"text":"श्रोत्रमध्यात्ममित्याहुर्यथाश्रुतिनिदर्शनम् ।\nशब्दस्तत्राधिभूतं तु दिशस्तत्राधिदैवतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the tradition teaches, the ear is called Self-related, sound here the elemental, and the directions the divinity there."}},{"n":8,"text":"जिह्वामध्यात्ममित्याहुर्यथातत्त्वनिदर्शनम् ।\nरस एवाधिभूतं तु आपस्तत्राधिदैवतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the principles teach, the tongue is called Self-related, taste itself the elemental, and the waters the divinity there."}},{"n":9,"text":"घ्राणमध्यात्ममित्याहुर्यथाश्रुतिनिदर्शनम् ।\nगन्ध एवाधिभूतं तु पृथिवी चाधिदैवतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the tradition teaches, the nose is called Self-related, smell itself the elemental, and Earth the divinity."}},{"n":10,"text":"त्वगध्यात्ममिति प्राहुस्तत्त्वबुद्धिविशारदाः ।\nस्पर्श एवाधिभूतं तु पवनश्चाधिदैवतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those skilled in the intellect of principles call the skin Self-related, touch itself the elemental, and the wind the divinity."}},{"n":11,"text":"मनोऽध्यात्ममिति प्राहुर्यथाश्रुतिनिदर्शनम् ।\nमन्तव्यमधिभूतं तु चन्द्रमाश्चाधिदैवतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the tradition teaches, the mind is called Self-related, what is to be thought the elemental, and the Moon the divinity."}},{"n":12,"text":"अहंकारिकमध्यात्ममाहुस्तत्त्वनिदर्शनम् ।\nअभिमानोऽधिभूतं तु भवस्तत्राधिदैवतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wise call the egoistic Self-related, as the principles teach; self-regard is the elemental, and Bhava the divinity there."}},{"n":13,"text":"बुद्धिरध्यात्ममित्याहुर्यथावेदनिदर्शनम् ।\nबोद्धव्यमधिभूतं तु क्षेत्रज्ञोऽत्राधिदैवतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the Veda teaches, the intellect is called Self-related, what is to be known the elemental, and the knower of the field the divinity here."}},{"n":14,"text":"एषा ते व्यक्ततो राजन्विभूतिरनुवर्णिता ।\nआदौ मध्ये तथा चान्ते यथातत्त्वेन तत्त्ववित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, this glory of the manifest has been described to you, at beginning, middle and end, as it truly is, by one who knows the truth."}},{"n":15,"text":"प्रकृतिर्गुणान्विकुरुते स्वच्छन्देनात्मकाम्यया ।\nक्रीडार्थं तु महाराज शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nature, of her own free will and for her own wish, transforms the qualities, hundreds and thousands of times, king, for play."}},{"n":16,"text":"यथा दीपसहस्राणि दीपान्मर्त्याः प्रकुर्वते ।\nप्रकृतिस्तथा विकुरुते पुरुषस्य गुणान्बहून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As mortals make thousands of lamps from one lamp, so Nature produces many qualities of the Person."}},{"n":17,"text":"सत्त्वमानन्द उद्रेकः प्रीतिः प्राकाश्यमेव च ।\nसुखं शुद्धित्वमारोग्यं संतोषः श्रद्दधानता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Goodness: joy, abundance, delight, illumination, happiness, purity, health, contentment, faith..."}},{"n":18,"text":"अकार्पण्यमसंरम्भः क्षमा धृतिरहिंसता ।\nसमता सत्यमानृण्यं मार्दवं ह्रीरचापलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"...generosity, calm, patience, steadiness, harmlessness, equanimity, truth, freedom from debt, gentleness, modesty, steadiness of mind..."}},{"n":19,"text":"शौचमार्जवमाचारमलौल्यं हृद्यसंभ्रमः ।\nइष्टानिष्टवियोगानां कृतानामविकत्थनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"...cleanness, uprightness, good conduct, freedom from greed, a gladdened heart, not boasting of deeds done or of the loss of what is liked or disliked..."}},{"n":20,"text":"दानेन चानुग्रहणमस्पृहार्थे परार्थता ।\nसर्वभूतदया चैव सत्त्वस्यैते गुणाः स्मृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"...helping through gifts, working for others without desire for gain, and compassion for all beings: these are held to be the qualities of goodness."}},{"n":21,"text":"रजोगुणानां संघातो रूपमैश्वर्यविग्रहे ।\nअत्याशित्वमकारुण्यं सुखदुःखोपसेवनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The group of the qualities of passion is beauty, power, and quarrelsomeness, overeating, cruelty, and indulgence in pleasure and pain."}},{"n":22,"text":"परापवादेषु रतिर्विवादानां च सेवनम् ।\nअहंकारस्त्वसत्कारश्चिन्ता वैरोपसेवनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Delight in slander of others, indulgence in disputes, egoism, disrespect, worry, and keeping enmity..."}},{"n":23,"text":"परितापोऽपहरणं ह्रीनाशोऽनार्जवं तथा ।\nभेदः परुषता चैव कामक्रोधौ मदस्तथा ।\nदर्पो द्वेषोऽतिवादश्च एते प्रोक्ता रजोगुणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"...remorse, theft, loss of shame, crookedness, division, harshness, desire, anger, intoxication, pride, hatred and overtalk: these are said to be the qualities of passion."}},{"n":24,"text":"तामसानां तु संघातं प्रवक्ष्याम्युपधार्यताम् ।\nमोहोऽप्रकाशस्तामिस्रमन्धतामिस्रसंज्ञितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Now I shall describe the group of the qualities of darkness; listen. Delusion, lack of light, and what are called tamisra and andhatamisra."}},{"n":25,"text":"मरणं चान्धतामिस्रं तामिस्रं क्रोध उच्यते ।\nतमसो लक्षणानीह भक्षाणामभिरोचनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Death is andhatamisra, and anger is called tamisra. Here the marks of darkness are a liking for things to eat..."}},{"n":26,"text":"भोजनानामपर्याप्तिस्तथा पेयेष्वतृप्तता ।\nगन्धवासो विहारेषु शयनेष्वासनेषु च ॥","meaning":{"en":"...never being satisfied with food or drink, fondness for perfumes in pleasures, beds and seats..."}},{"n":27,"text":"दिवास्वप्ने विवादे च प्रमादेषु च वै रतिः ।\nनृत्यवादित्रगीतानामज्ञानाच्छ्रद्दधानता ।\nद्वेषो धर्मविशेषाणामेते वै तामसा गुणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"...love of sleeping by day, of quarrels and of heedlessness, faith in dance, music and song through ignorance, and hatred of special forms of dharma: these are the qualities of darkness."}}]}]}